    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee is neither confirmed against the rider nor refunded to them. The amount is held for a human reviewer.\n\nWhat the record does establish. The cancellation came at 08:51:00 with a 5.00 SGD fee charged (EV-FARE-00903, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0) — the exact fee POL-NS-22 fixes, so the fee-amount check raises nothing. The free wait was served: the trip was scheduled for 08:45:00 and the driver arrived before it, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s wait ran 08:45:00–08:50:00 and the 08:51:00 cancellation fell after it (EV-TRIP-00903 free_wait check true). The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 was met: four in-app messages (08:43:00, 08:45:20, 08:49:30, 08:50:45) and one in-app call at 08:47:05 ringing 22 s unanswered, all before cancelled_at (EV-TRIP-00903, EV-CHAT-00903). The rider's account — that they were at the lobby and the driver never came — is carried by nothing: the GPS rider_track is empty and the chat log holds no rider message. So POL-NS-24's full-refund route is not open either, and its 5.00 SGD goodwill credit does not arise because contact was attempted.\n\nWhat the record cannot do. The case turns on the driver's arrival, and the only thing placing the driver at the pickup is a GPS measurement. The trip record's 08:43:00 arrival marker was auto-confirmed from that same fix (EV-TRIP-00903 event detail), so under POL-GEN-02 the marker and EV-GPS-00903 are one carrier, not two. That carrier is impaired: EV-GPS-00903 weighs 0.6 with issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD. EV-TRIP-00903 (1.0), EV-CHAT-00903 (1.0) and EV-FARE-00903 (0.75) do not lift it — the driver's own chat messages are his own assertions, not an independent measurement, and the fare ledger only records the fee. Under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence on that fact cannot exceed 0.6.\n\nThe rider's profile carries fraud_flags = 1, so POL-GEN-22 requires a confidence of 0.95 for any AI ruling here whatever the 5.00 SGD value, and POL-NS-26 makes a no-show ruling final only subject to that 0.95. A ceiling of 0.6 cannot reach 0.95, and POL-GEN-26 names 'when the driver arrived' as a fact that must go to a human reviewer when the evidence carrying it is impaired. I therefore cannot confirm the 5.00 SGD fee against the rider, and equally cannot find for the rider that the driver never came. The driver's request for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD fails on this bar, not on the merits; the rider's request that the charge be reversed fails for the same reason.\n\nNo referral arises: the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not fire (contact was attempted), the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show counter is not present on the rider profile, and the charge is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 fixes, so no fee-amount referral under POL-NS-22. Open question for the reviewer: can the driver's auto-confirmed 08:43:00 arrival, and the rider's claimed presence, be resolved when no fix on the trace reports a horizontal accuracy?"
