    "explanation": "To both parties: this no-show charge cannot be finally decided by the AI on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer. The disputed 5.00 SGD cancellation fee is held — it is neither refunded to the rider nor released to the driver — until that review.\n\nWhat the record shows. The rider was charged a 5.00 SGD cancellation fee (EV-FARE-00903) after driver D-2398 marked arrival at 08:43:00 and cancelled at 08:51:00 (EV-TRIP-00903). The scheduled pickup was 08:45:00. Because the driver arrived before the scheduled time, POL-NS-21 fixes the 300 s free wait from the scheduled time, i.e. 08:45:00 to 08:50:00; the cancellation at 08:51:00 came after it (EV-TRIP-00903, free_wait check cancelled_after_free_wait true, seconds_from_start_to_cancel 360.0). Before cancelling, the driver sent four in-app messages (08:43:00, 08:45:20, 08:49:30, 08:50:45) and placed one in-app call at 08:47:05 that rang 22 s unanswered (EV-CHAT-00903, EV-TRIP-00903), so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is met. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD fee in force (EV-FARE-00903, fee_matches_policy true). POL-NS-24 gives no route to a refund: the driver arrived at 08:43:00, seven minutes inside the 08:50:00 deadline (arrived_by_deadline true), and contacted the rider, so neither the full refund nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit arises. On those facts the driver's side (claims that arrival is met, the free wait served, the contact obligation satisfied, POL-NS-24 closed, and the fee equal to the fee in force) is accepted.\n\nWhy the AI still cannot rule. The fact this case turns on — whether the driver was actually at the pickup — rests on the GPS trace EV-GPS-00903, which is impaired at weight 0.6 (issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD): its sampling gaps inside the waiting window exceed the 120 s policy threshold. The trip record's own arrival marker was auto-generated from that same GPS measurement ('Auto-arrival confirmed', EV-TRIP-00903), so under POL-GEN-02 the marker and the trace are one carrier, not two, and the trace's 0.6 is the ceiling for the arrival fact. The fare ledger EV-FARE-00903 is also impaired at 0.75 (PARTIAL_RECORD). The driver's submission that the deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-00903 and EV-CHAT-00903 at weight 1.0 is accepted for the free-wait and contact facts but rejected for arrival: the marker merely restates the impaired GPS measurement and does not lift the cap. The rider's submission that the rider's own presence is untested (the trace's rider_track is empty and the chat log holds no rider message) is noted and is a further open question for the reviewer.\n\nUnder POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence cannot exceed 0.6, and because the rider's profile carries a fraud flag of 1 (EV-RPROF-00903), POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 require a confidence of 0.95 whatever the dispute value. The record cannot reach that bar, so the ruling is ESCALATE and the amount is held; no monetary outcome issues.\n\nNo referral arises. The fee charged is exactly 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check produces none; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not apply because the driver both arrived by the deadline and attempted contact; and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not apply because the rider profile carries no no-show counter (the field is absent, and POL-NS-25 acts only when it is present).",
